+		c.mu.Unlock()
+	}

TryLogout forgets the node key only when control confirmed the logout. Upstream
also forgets it after a failed request; the map poll continues and saves the
empty key over the stored login, leaving the node registered at control with no
local key with which to log out again.

--- a/ipn/ipnlocal/local.go
+++ b/ipn/ipnlocal/local.go
@@ -2081,1 +2081,6 @@
 		b.mu.Lock()
+		if b.cc != c {
+			// A logout or profile change replaced the client while unlocked.
+			b.logf("Ignoring SetControlClientStatus from old client")
+			return
+		}

setControlClientStatusLocked unlocks while handling a network map for tailnet
lock. A logout in that window deletes the profile and replaces the control
client; upstream then installs the old network map on the logged-out profile,
which reports Stopped with the old addresses. The status is now ignored, as
upstream already does for an old client's status on entry.
